    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d623">

                <pb facs="0644" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg632"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Hamilton, Maxwell M./9–1945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hulley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-19T17:00:00-04:00">September 19,
                            1945—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>152. Please request <hi rendition="#italic">agrément</hi> of Finnish Govt for the
                    Honorable Maxwell M. Hamilton as Envoy Extraordinary and Minister
                    Plenipotentiary near the Finnish Govt. Dept should be informed by telegraph as
                    soon as <hi rendition="#italic">agrément</hi> has been given.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d623-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d623-f1" n="9" xml:id="d623-f1-content">
                <p>The Finnish Government’s <hi rendition="#italic">agrément</hi> was received on
                    October 4, 1945. Mr. Hamilton presented his credentials on March 4, 1946.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
